ARCHITECTURE — web composition reproduced exactly (WidgetShell + FleetStatsBar)
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
The web source is a thin wrapper:

    export default function FleetStatsWidget(_props) {
      ...useVehicles / useFleetAnalytics(30) / useUnits / useQuery(recent drives|charges)...
      return <WidgetShell noPadding updatedAt isFetching isStale isError onRefresh>
               <FleetStatsBar analytics vehicleCount onlineCount unreadAlerts
                              recentDrives recentCharges toDistanceDisplay
                              toEfficiencyDisplay distanceUnit efficiencyUnit />
             </WidgetShell>;
    }

The native `FleetStatsBar` leaf ALREADY exists as the verified feature-view surface 0123
(apps/apple/TeslaSync/feature-views/FleetStatsBar.*): the five-card grid, both Swift-Charts
sparklines, every load/freshness state, the P1/S8 state holder (FleetStatsBarModel /
FleetStatsSource / InMemoryFleetStatsSource), the P1/S10 parity strings (table "FleetStatsBar")
and the a11y summaries. So this widget reproduces the web composition 1:1: it COMPOSES the shared
`FleetStatsBar` (it does NOT re-implement the cards — DRY, no drift) and adds the `WidgetShell`
chrome the web wraps it in (the glass container + the title-less `DataFreshness` refresh control),
the canonical `fleet-stats` registry registration, and the widget-slug `view.opened` telemetry.

